# Copy to .env (gitignored) on the infra VM, or let scripts/init-vaultwarden.sh
# seed it. The script generates the database password; the admin token is
# minted by hand — see docs/vaultwarden-setup.md, step 3.

# Password for Vaultwarden's dedicated Postgres. Generated by the init script
# when blank, as HEX (openssl rand -hex 32) rather than base64 like the other
# stacks: this value is also substituted into DATABASE_URL, which is a URI, and
# base64's + / = would need percent-encoding there. Hex needs none.
# NOTE: Postgres keeps the password its data dir was FIRST initialized with; on
# an existing deployment this must match that value.
VAULTWARDEN_DB_PASSWORD=

# Argon2id PHC hash of the /admin password. NOT generated by the init script —
# `vaultwarden hash` prompts for the password twice and needs a terminal:
#   docker run --rm -it vaultwarden/server:1.37.1 /vaultwarden hash
#
# SINGLE-QUOTE the value, exactly as printed. Compose interpolates unquoted and
# double-quoted .env values, so the $argon2id$v=19$... string would lose every
# $-segment and the admin page would then reject the password you just typed.
# Keep the password itself in the vault once the vault exists — this line is
# the hash, and the hash cannot get you back in.
VAULTWARDEN_ADMIN_TOKEN=
